  "notes": [
   "The parts list is the same as in step 1. Nothing was added or dropped.",
   "The wiring diagram image was not available, so the wiring follows the text. The text says the relay is powered from the Nano Matter 3.3V pin and controlled from D4, and that the relay must interrupt the AC current path.",
   "Nano Matter breadboard placement is assumed. It sits across the centre gap in columns 1-15, with the standard Nano pin layout: 3V3 at column 2 on the top half, GND at column 4 and D4 at column 7 on the bottom half. Jumper wires go into the same column strips as those pins.",
   "The Grove relay module is not plugged into the breadboard. Its Grove pins (GND, VCC, SIG) are reached by three jumper wires, which stand in for the coloured Grove cable seen in the photo.",
   "AC path: cable live (L) goes to relay COM. Relay NO goes to socket terminal 1, and socket terminal 2 goes back to the cable neutral (N). When the relay is open the circuit is broken. The bulb is screwed into the socket, so its leads are joined to socket terminals 1 and 2.",
   "The plug end of the AC cable goes to the wall outlet, which is not a part. The far end of the USB-C cable goes to a power source that the tutorial does not list, so no edge was added for it.",
   "The Nest Hub has no edge because it links to the Nano Matter only wirelessly, over Thread and Matter. It is kept as a part because the parts list names it.",
   "The orange wire nut seen in the photo is not in the parts list, so it is omitted."
  ]
 },
